
                       8Ball for Teleconference
                   for The Major BBS v10 - version 1.0.0

              Copyright (c) 2026 Elwynor Technologies.
   Originally HOTELeconference 8Ball by Randall R. Spangler, annex.com.
     8Ball converted for The Major BBS v10 by Mark Laudenbach -
                    https://github.com/laudenbachm


WHAT IT DOES
------------

The Magic 8-Ball for the stock Teleconference.  In any channel, type

     8BALL Should I log off now?

You see the 8-Ball picture with its answer inside.  Everyone else in the
channel sees one line of chat from you, such as

     From Mark: [Magic 8-Ball] "Should I log off now?" ... Outlook Good

Because the answer is sent as ordinary chat, it also reaches users on
other boards in a linked channel, such as MajorLink.  Those boards don't
need 8Ball installed.

     8BALL              shake it without a question
     8BALL ?            help (8BALL HELP works too)

Each user can ask once every 30 seconds (the Sysop can change this).


INSTALLING
----------

1. Shut down the BBS.
2. Copy ELW8BTEL.DLL, ELW8BTEL.MDF, ELW8BTEL.MSG and ELW8BTEL.RLN into the
   BBS folder.
3. Start the BBS.  The module loads by itself (it has no menu entry) and
   adds the 8BALL command to Teleconference.  The Audit Trail shows
   "8BALL FOR TELECONFERENCE  v1.0.0 loaded (command 8BALL)".

The module needs Teleconference (GALTELE).  If Teleconference isn't
installed, the Audit Trail says "8BALL NOT STARTED" with the version and
the reason, and the rest of the board runs as normal.

The settings file, ELW8BTEL.DAT, is created on the first start.

The module is a 32-bit (Win32) DLL, like The Major BBS v10 itself.  It runs
on 64-bit Windows.


SETTINGS (SYSOPS)
-----------------

Settings are changed online, while the board runs.  Changes take effect
immediately and are written to the Audit Trail.  There are no
configuration editor options.  In Teleconference, a user with the SYSOP
key types

     8BALL SET                    list the settings
     8BALL SET <number> <value>   change one
     8BALL SET DEFAULTS           put them all back to the defaults

  1. 8-Ball answers questions          YES or NO.  Default YES.
  2. Key to use the 8-Ball             A key or lock expression.  Blank
                                       (the default) lets everyone use it.
                                       Enter - to blank it.
  3. Key to pick a reply and skip      Default SYSOP.  Blank = nobody.
     the wait                          A holder can also type
                                       8BALL /REPLY3 question
                                       to get reply 3.
  4. Seconds a user waits between      0 to 3600.  Default 30.
     uses
  5. Channels it works in              Channel names separated by
                                       commas, for example
                                       Main, MajorLink
                                       Blank (the default) or * means
                                       every channel.  Enter - to blank it.

Users who are squelched in Teleconference can't use the 8-Ball.


CHANGING THE TEXT AND ANSWERS
-----------------------------

All text is in ELW8BTEL.MSG (configuration editor, level 6).  Values are
named text variables (E8B_QUESTION, E8B_ANSWER and so on), so the text
can be reworded freely.  Changes to the .MSG take effect after the BBS is
restarted.

The answers are REPLY01 to REPLY30.  21 are filled in.  Each is written

     first line|second line

which are the two lines shown inside the 8-Ball picture (12 characters
each fit).  Everyone else sees them joined with a space.  Blank replies
are skipped, so you add or remove answers just by editing the text.  Keep
each answer under 80 characters and in plain text.

PUBQ and PUBNQ are the line the channel sees.  Keep them to one plain
line: boards on the other end of a link may not show colors the way yours
does.

Note: copying a new ELW8BTEL.MSG over the old one replaces any text you
changed in it.


VERSION HISTORY
---------------

1.0.0 (19 October 2026)

  First release for The Major BBS v10, converted from HOTELeconference
  8Ball 2.00 (1997).
  - Works in the stock Teleconference, including web users and linked
    channels such as MajorLink.
  - Online settings (8BALL SET) instead of configuration editor options.
  - Choose which channels the 8-Ball works in.
  - Answers can be added or removed just by editing the text.
